        "docxContentHtml": "<div class='overflow-x-auto my-3'><table class='min-w-full text-xs border border-slate-200 divide-y divide-slate-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden bg-white'><tr><th class='px-3 py-2 font-bold bg-slate-50 text-slate-700 border-r border-slate-200'>LAB 211 Assignment</th><th class='px-3 py-2 font-bold bg-slate-50 text-slate-700 border-r border-slate-200'>Type:</th><th class='px-3 py-2 font-bold bg-slate-50 text-slate-700 border-r border-slate-200'>Long Assignment</th></tr><tr><td class='px-3 py-2 text-slate-600 border-r border-slate-100'></td><td class='px-3 py-2 text-slate-600 border-r border-slate-100'>Code:</td><td class='px-3 py-2 text-slate-600 border-r border-slate-100'>J1.L.P0038</td></tr><tr><td class='px-3 py-2 text-slate-600 border-r border-slate-100'></td><td class='px-3 py-2 text-slate-600 border-r border-slate-100'>LOC:</td><td class='px-3 py-2 text-slate-600 border-r border-slate-100'>300</td></tr><tr><td class='px-3 py-2 text-slate-600 border-r border-slate-100'></td><td class='px-3 py-2 text-slate-600 border-r border-slate-100'>Slot(s):</td><td class='px-3 py-2 text-slate-600 border-r border-slate-100'>5</td></tr></table></div><p class='text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed my-1.5'><b>Title:</b> Car insurance Management</p><h4 class='text-sm font-black text-slate-800 mt-4 mb-2 flex items-center gap-2'><span class='w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-blue-500 inline-block'></span>Background Context</h4><p class='text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed my-1.5'>Write a program to manage car insurance implementing the Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) paradigm. In this assignment, we will use the Map&lt;Key, Value&gt; structure to store a collection of objects (Key is identity, Value is object).</p><h4 class='text-sm font-black text-slate-800 mt-4 mb-2 flex items-center gap-2'><span class='w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-blue-500 inline-block'></span>Program Specifications (10 Functions)</h4><div class='p-2.5 my-1.5 rounded-lg bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80 font-medium text-xs text-slate-700'>1. Add car information (License plate unique, owner 2-35 chars, value > 999, registration date, seats 5/7/9)</div><div class='p-2.5 my-1.5 rounded-lg bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80 font-medium text-xs text-slate-700'>2. Find a car by license plate</div><div class='p-2.5 my-1.5 rounded-lg bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80 font-medium text-xs text-slate-700'>3. Update car information (all fields except license plate)</div><div class='p-2.5 my-1.5 rounded-lg bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80 font-medium text-xs text-slate-700'>4. Delete a car (prevent deletion if car is registered in insurance)</div><div class='p-2.5 my-1.5 rounded-lg bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80 font-medium text-xs text-slate-700'>5. Add an insurance statement</div><div class='p-2.5 my-1.5 rounded-lg bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80 font-medium text-xs text-slate-700'>6. List of insurance statements</div><div class='p-2.5 my-1.5 rounded-lg bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80 font-medium text-xs text-slate-700'>7. Report on uninsured cars</div><div class='p-2.5 my-1.5 rounded-lg bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80 font-medium text-xs text-slate-700'>8. Save data</div><div class='p-2.5 my-1.5 rounded-lg bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80 font-medium text-xs text-slate-700'>9. Load data</div>",
